## §2 — PLAN

### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
Top-level: `stageW 640 · stageH 400 · boardX 40 · boardY 96 · boardW 560 · boardH 264 · boardRadiusPx 26 · domeCx 320 · domeCy 300 · domeR 92 · stripCount 3 · stripGapPx 10 · sliceDurMs 1400 · sawAmpPx 7 · sawCycles 3 · tHoldStripsMs 1400 · knifeRestX 96 · knifeRestY 64 · chopLeadMs 420 · chopTravelPx 118 · settleFrac 0.12 · settleDurMs 400 · holdMs 500 · seed 23209 · easeChop "easeIn" · easeSettle "easeInOut" · fontFamily "Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif" (comparison/labels only — the recreation itself carries no text)`.
Dice passes (nested CONFIG array `passes[]` — `{tMs, count, sizeFactor, layout, scatterRadiusPx}`; count = cumulative total AFTER the pass; sizeFactor applies to the dice that pass ADDS; layout "stack" = grid layers, "pile" = seeded scatter):
- passes[0] `{tMs 2500, count 9, sizeFactor 1.00, layout "stack", scatterRadiusPx 0}` — the literalization landing (SB-B)
- passes[1] `{tMs 3500, count 15, sizeFactor 1.00, layout "stack", scatterRadiusPx 0}` — stack growth (SB-C)
- passes[2] `{tMs 4500, count 18, sizeFactor 0.94, layout "stack", scatterRadiusPx 0}` — stack growth (SB-C)
- passes[3] `{tMs 5600, count 56, sizeFactor 0.60, layout "pile", scatterRadiusPx 128}` — multiplication chop (SB-D)
- passes[4] `{tMs 6500, count 84, sizeFactor 0.38, layout "pile", scatterRadiusPx 168}` — final spread (SB-E)
Die geometry: `dieBasePx 37 · dieRadiusPx 6 · pipRadiusFrac 0.11 · stackColGapPx 3 · stackRowGapPx 3`.
Palette: `{ground #17110b, board #8a6844, boardEdge #5d4126, boardGrain #77572f, leather #f2ede2, stitch #b3392f, yarn #6e6259, ring #c8452c, core #a9805a, dice #ffffff, diceEdge #c9c9c9, pip #1c1c1c, steel #c8ccd2, steelDark #9aa0a8, handle #4a3220}`.
Derived (named, not stored): dice added by pass i = passes[i].count − passes[i−1].count (pass 0: passes[0].count) · die size for a die added by pass i = dieBasePx × passes[i].sizeFactor · pip face per die = seeded value 1–6 (mulberry32 on CONFIG seed, die index order) · scatter position per pile die = seeded point inside the pass's scatter ellipse, stack position per stack die = grid (column, row, layer) in index order · swap instant = passes[0].tMs · completeAtMs = passes[last].tMs + settleDurMs · durationMs = completeAtMs + holdMs = 6500 + 400 + 500 = 7400 ≤ 8000 (segment span incl. handles) ✓.
**Phase-order invariant (validation-enforced):** sliceDurMs ≤ tHoldStripsMs ≤ passes[0].tMs · passes tMs strictly increasing · passes counts strictly increasing · every sizeFactor ∈ (0, 1] · chopLeadMs < smallest inter-pass gap. A CONFIG violating the order is rejected by validateConfig, never rendered overlapped.

### 2.2 Construction choice
**DOM/SVG shapes + one pure evaluator (chosen):** one SVG scene — board rect with grain lines, a dome group of `stripCount` strip paths (vertical slices of a half-disc, stitch dashes on the arcs, cut-face bands), a knife group (blade polygon + handle), and one rect+pip-circles group per die — all geometry from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node (window.__T232). Dice positions are computed inside stateAt from the seeded RNG so the harness counts and measures the exact built set.
Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element DOM measurement the A6 fit leg and harness receipts use. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). Traced/photographic assets — refusal-class under §6.1. A physics/scatter simulation — the specimen's landings are stop-motion steps, not continuous physics; a simulation would invent motion the census does not show.

